  title: Warmer seas, stronger typhoons
  body: "Typhoons draw their energy from warm ocean water. Typhoons that hit East
    and Southeast Asia have become 12\u201315% stronger since the late 1970s, as
    the seas near these coasts warmed. A warmer ocean feeds stronger storms."
